{
 "note": "One night out: neon-lit people, crowds, a DJ, sparklers. Chosen so that consecutive shots belong to the same party and most of them contain a person, because faces are where the feeling is.",
 "made_by": {
  "how": "curated",
  "who": "a person looking at a contact sheet of 70 party/dance/people clips",
  "not": "NOT selected by the system, and this is the second set curated this way. The measurements cannot do it: a club crowd and a star field are both dark, and the source's category names are worse -- 'dance' contained a man asleep in bed. The previous curated set had only three or four clips with a person in them, so the chooser collapsed onto those and the edit repeated four clips thirteen times.",
  "what_would_replace_it": "A text-aligned image embedding, so that observations.mood -- already a text-aligned MUSIC embedding -- could pick footage in the same space."
 },
